    "description": "# Future Directions\n\nFive falsifiable conjectures distilled from what survived, and what resisted, in this cycle.\nEach is stated so that it can be written down as a Lean 4 theorem on top of the definitions\nalready in `Catalog/Physics/EntanglementMonotone/`.\n\nBackground actually established (all sorry-free): the variational trace norm\n`\u2016X\u2016\u2081 = inf {tr P + tr Q : X = P \u2212 Q, P,Q \u2ab0 0}` equals `\u2211\u1d62|\u03bb\u1d62|`; both the primal infimum and\nthe dual supremum `sup {Re tr(XW) : \u22121 \u2aaf W \u2aaf 1}` are attained; `E_N = log\u2016\u0393\u03c1\u2016\u2081` is monotone\nunder PPT operations (hence under LOCC), strongly monotone under PPT instruments, vanishes\nexactly on PPT states, is additive under tensor products, is bounded by `\u00bd log(d_A d_B)`, and\nattains that bound only at the maximally entangled state.\n\n---\n\n## Conjecture 1 (Exact duality formula for the monotone)\n\n`E_N(\u03c1) = log (max {Re tr(\u0393\u03c1 \u00b7 W) : W Hermitian, \u22121 \u2aaf W \u2aaf 1})`, and the maximising `W` may\nalways be taken of the form `\u0393(entanglement witness)`; consequently `E_N` extends to a\nPPT-monotone functional on the whole real vector space of Hermitian operators, not just\nstates, that is *concave along the PPT boundary*.\n\n**The key insight is** that strong duality \u2014 proved here in the form\n`exists_contraction_traceNorm_eq` \u2014 turns the monotone from an infimum (hard to bound from\nbelow) into a maximum over a *compact convex* set of certificates, so every lower bound on\nentanglement becomes an explicit finite-dimensional witness, and witness geometry (a convex\ngeometry question) becomes directly available to the trace-norm theory (an operator-algebra\nquestion).\n\n**Why now?** The attainment statement, which is the analytic obstruction, is now formalised;\nwhat remains is convex geometry of the contraction ball, for which Mathlib's convexity and\ncompactness libraries are already adequate.\n\n## Conjecture 2 (Rigidity of the maximiser)\n\nOn `\u2102^d \u2297 \u2102^d`, `E_N(\u03c1) = log d` **only** for maximally entangled states: if `E_N(\u03c1) = log d`\nthen `\u03c1 = (U \u2297 V) \u03a6_d (U \u2297 V)\u1d34` for local unitaries `U, V`.\n\n**The key insight is** that the Cauchy\u2013Schwarz step `\u2211|\u03bb\u1d62| \u2264 \u221aN \u221a(\u2211\u03bb\u1d62\u00b2)` used in\n`logNeg_le_log_dim` is an equality only when all `|\u03bb\u1d62|` coincide, and the purity step\n`tr \u03c1\u00b2 \u2264 1` is an equality only for pure states; chaining the two equality cases forces the\npartial transpose to have flat spectrum `\u00b11/d`, which is a rigidity statement about the\nswap operator.\n\n**Why now?** The inequality chain is already formalised as a chain of named lemmas, so the\nconjecture reduces to the equality analysis of two standard inequalities \u2014 no new analytic\ninput is required, only the equality conditions.\n\n## Conjecture 3 (Asymptotic distillation and irreversibility)\n\nFor every state `\u03c1`, and every `n, m` with an *exact* PPT protocol `\u039b` mapping `\u03c1^{\u2297n}` to\n`\u03a6_{2^m}`, one has `m log 2 \u2264 n E_N(\u03c1)`; moreover there exist states (PPT-entangled ones) for\nwhich the entanglement *cost* under PPT operations is strictly positive while this\ndistillation rate is `0`, so the PPT theory of entanglement is irreversible.\n\n**The key insight is** that additivity plus monotonicity already give the single-shot rate\nbound (formalised here for two copies as\n`log_card_le_logNeg_of_exact_two_copy_distillation`), so irreversibility becomes a *separation*\nstatement between two quantities that both sandwich `E_N`, rather than a new asymptotic\nanalysis.\n\n**Why now?** The `n = 2` case is proved; the general `n` case needs only a coherent\nformalisation of iterated tensor regrouping (an `Equiv`-bookkeeping problem), which the\n`regroup`/`tensorBipartite` machinery of this cycle already makes routine.\n\n## Conjecture 4 (Continuity with an explicit modulus)\n\n`|E_N(\u03c1) \u2212 E_N(\u03c3)| \u2264 log(1 + d\u2016\u03c1 \u2212 \u03c3\u2016\u2081)`, and this modulus is optimal up to a constant; in\nparticular `E_N` is continuous but *not* asymptotically continuous with a dimension-free\nmodulus.\n\n**The key insight is** that `\u0393` is an isometry for the Hilbert\u2013Schmidt norm (proved here as\n`trace_ptrans_sq`) but only a `d`-bounded map for the trace norm, and the logarithm converts\nthis multiplicative distortion into an additive modulus; the failure of dimension-free\ncontinuity is therefore traceable to a single norm-equivalence constant.\n\n**Why now?** Both norms and their comparison are already formalised in this development, and\nthe estimate `|log x \u2212 log y| \u2264 |x \u2212 y| / min(x,y)` with `\u2016\u0393\u03c1\u2016\u2081 \u2265 1` closes the gap with\nMathlib's existing logarithm lemmas.\n\n## Conjecture 5 (Multipartite monogamy)\n\nFor a tripartite state on `\u2102^A \u2297 \u2102^B \u2297 \u2102^C`, the negativities across the three bipartite cuts\nsatisfy a monogamy inequality `N_{A|BC}\u00b2 \u2265 N_{A|B}\u00b2 + N_{A|C}\u00b2`, with equality exactly for\ngeneralised GHZ-type states.\n\n**The key insight is** that the covariance identity `\u0393((A\u2297B)X(A\u2297B)\u1d34) = (A\u2297B\u0304)(\u0393X)(A\u2297B\u0304)\u1d34`\nproved here for the bipartite cut applies verbatim to each cut of a multipartite system once\ntensor factors are regrouped, so monogamy becomes a statement about how three different\npartial transposes of the *same* matrix constrain each other \u2014 a genuinely combinatorial\nconstraint on a single spectrum.\n\n**Why now?** The regrouping equivalences (`regroup`, `tensorBipartite`) and the spectral\nidentification of the trace norm make each cut computable from a common spectral object, so\nthe conjecture can be tested exhaustively on small dimensions with the exact rational\n`#eval` methodology already used in `ComputationalEvidence.md` before any proof attempt.\n\n---\n\n### Three concrete next-cycle sub-conjectures\n\n1. **(N1)** `\u2016X \u2297 Y\u2016\u2081 = \u2016X\u2016\u2081\u2016Y\u2016\u2081` extends from Hermitian to arbitrary complex matrices once\n   the trace norm is defined through `\u221a(X\u1d34X)`; the variational definition used here is the\n   Hermitian shadow of that statement.\n2. **(N2)** The set `{\u03c1 : E_N(\u03c1) = 0}` is exactly the PPT cone intersected with the state\n   space and is *strictly larger* than the separable set in every dimension `d_A d_B \u2265 6`\n   (existence of bound entanglement).\n3. **(N3)** Selective monotonicity (`logNeg_strong_mono`) is tight: for every `\u03b5 > 0` there is\n   a PPT instrument whose average output negativity is within `\u03b5` of the input's, so no\n   strictly-decreasing refinement of the monotone exists on the whole state space.\n",
