    "description": "**Conjecture.** A weight-graded dg-algebra `A` is pure if and only if the inclusion of the\ndiagonal cocycle subalgebra `diagAlg \u2286 A` (already constructed, with zero differential) induces\na *surjection* on cohomology in every degree **and** the off-diagonal part of `A` is exact as a\ncomplex in each fixed weight. In particular purity is equivalent to a statement about a single\nstrict subalgebra, with no reference to truncations.\n\n*The key insight is* that `diagAlg \u2192 H(A)` is always multiplicative and its surjectivity is the\nonly place where purity was used in `diagonal_strict_section`; the converse direction should\nrecover weight-wise acyclicity from surjectivity plus a dimension/graded-Nakayama argument.\n\n*Why now?* `diagSubalg_surjective_on_cohomology` supplies one direction verbatim; the converse\nis a finite bookkeeping statement about the same objects. Falsifiable by an example where\n`diagAlg` surjects on cohomology but some off-diagonal weight-complex has cohomology.",
