    "description": "**Statement.** For `T` a real M\u00f6bius map of positive determinant and `S` a\nmeasurable subset of the upper half-plane,\n`\u222b_{T(S)} dx dy/y\u00b2 = \u222b_S dx dy/y\u00b2`.\n\n*The key insight is* that `mobius_conformal_factor` already contains the\nproof: the real Jacobian of `T` viewed as a map `\u211d\u00b2 \u2192 \u211d\u00b2` is `\u2016T'(z)\u2016\u00b2`, and\n`Im T(z) = \u2016T'(z)\u2016 \u00b7 Im z` is exactly the statement proved, so the density\n`1/y\u00b2` transforms with the reciprocal of the Jacobian.  What remains is\nMathlib's change-of-variables theorem, not geometry.\n\n*Why now?* Mathlib has `MeasureTheory.integral_image_eq_integral_abs_det_fderiv_smul`;\nthe missing input was precisely the pointwise identity now proved.\n\n**Falsifiable form.** Apply `z \u21a6 -1/z` to the ideal triangle `(0,1,\u221e)`, whose\nimage is the ideal triangle `(\u221e,-1,0)`; the conjecture predicts both have area\n`\u03c0`.  Any numerically different value refutes it.",
