    "description": "**Statement.** Over the definitions `shuf` (shuffle) and `deconc`\n(deconcatenation coproduct) of `Catalog/Novelty/`, for every nonempty word `w`\nand every field `K \u2287 \u211a`,\n`\u03a3_{(u,v) \u2208 deconc w} (-1)^{|u|} \u00b7 (count z (shuf (reverse u) v)) = 0` for all\n`z`, i.e. `S(w) = (-1)^{|w|} \u00b7 reverse w` is the antipode of the graded Hopf\nalgebra `(K\u27e8X\u27e9, \u29e2, \u0394_deconc)`.\n\n*The key insight is* that the already-proved bialgebra axiom\n`deconc_bind_shuf` upgrades to a Hopf structure precisely because the\ndeconcatenation coproduct is connected and graded, so the antipode is forced by\nTakeuchi's recursion \u2014 and the closed form must then be a *signed multiset\nidentity between shuffles of reversals*, which is a purely combinatorial claim\namenable to the counting machinery (`count_shuf_eq_count_unsh`,\n`count_deconc`) already developed here.\n\n*Why now?* All of the counting infrastructure for `shuf`, `unsh` and `deconc`\nnow exists and is verified; the antipode is the last missing structure map, and\nit is exactly the input needed to state Sweedler duality intrinsically.\n\n---",
