    "description": "**Conjecture.** For a fixed `G`, the set of achievable pairs\n`(rate, information)` over *all* conjugation-stable forks and *all* moduli is the\nfinite set `{(|S|/|G|, H(pq) \u2212 p\u00b7H(q)) : S a union of G^ab-fibres thinned by a\nG-orbit}` \u2014 in particular it is contained in the curve family\n`I = H(pq) \u2212 p\u00b7H(q)` with `p \u2208 (1/[G:G'])\u00b7\u2124` and `q \u2208 (1/|G'|)\u00b7\u2124`.\n\n*The key insight is* that every fork factors as (pinned part) \u2218 (flat thinning),\nbecause the commutator subgroup acts transitively on the ambiguity: the leakage\nlaw is not one example but a normal form.\n*Why now?* `info_leak`, `info_leak_strict` and `abelian_hom_eq_one_on_V4` give\nthe two extremes; the missing step is a decomposition lemma \"every fork is a\n`q`-thinning of its `G^ab`-saturation\", which is a finite-group statement.",
