    "description": "**Conjecture.** For fixed `N` and `P` of infinite order, the set of primes `\u2113` for which the\napparition index is even has natural density `1/2` inside the primes; equivalently the parity of\n`ord(P mod \u2113)` equidistributes.\n\n*The key insight is* that the parity of the order of a reduction is governed by the splitting of\nthe `2`-division field of `E_N` \u2014 a Chebotarev condition \u2014 so the density is the proportion of\nFrobenius classes acting without fixed vector on `E[2]`.\n\n*Why now?* Cycle 7's density theorem gives the counting framework, and Mathlib's Galois and\nChebotarev-adjacent machinery has grown enough that the `2`-division field of a Mordell curve\n(a pure cubic extension) can be handled explicitly rather than abstractly.",
