    "consumed_by_exp_id": "",
    "description": "**Conjecture.** Let `L/\u211a` be Galois with group `G`, let `N \u22b4 G` with `G/N` cyclic\nof order `m`, and let `F = [Frob \u2208 N]`.  Then `F` is pinned by the character of\nconductor `f(G/N)` and `I(p mod f ; F) = H(1/m)` exactly; conversely, if a fork\nof rate `1/m` attains `I = H(1/m)` for some modulus, its defining set is a union\nof fibres of a cyclic quotient of order `m`.\n\n*The key insight is* that the entropy value `H(1/m)` is not a coincidence of the\ncubic case: it is the entropy of the uniform distribution on the fibres of\n`G \u21a0 G^ab \u21a0 C_m`, and the trichotomy theorem already forces saturation to be\nequivalent to determinism, so only the *rate* survives as an invariant.\n*Why now?* Both halves are now formal objects: `info_eq_top_iff` supplies the\nconverse direction abstractly, and `factorsThroughAb_iff` supplies the group\nside; only the Artin/Chebotarev bridge remains to be axiomatised or imported.",
