    "description": "**Conjecture.** For `N` a product of `k` unramified primes of the `A\u2084`-field,\nthe mutual information between `N mod 9` and the full split-vector satisfies\n`I_k = \u0398(k\u00b73^{-k})` for the \"all split\" fork and `I_k \u2192 H(Bin-class)` for the\ncount fork; in particular the *per-factor* information tends to `0`\ngeometrically, quantifying \"factor-useless\".\n\n*The key insight is* that thinning by `3^{-(k-1)}` sends the leakage law into the\nregime `H(pq) \u2212 pH(q) \u2248 pq\u00b7log\u2082(1/p)`, which is linear in `q`; the proved limit\n`info_all_split_tendsto_zero` is the qualitative shadow of that asymptotic.\n*Why now?* The exact `k`-dependent closed form `H(3^{-(k+1)}) \u2212 (1/3)H(3^{-k})`\nis already formal, so the conjecture is now a pure asymptotic analysis exercise\nabout `H` near `0`.",
