    "description": "**Conjecture.**  For every `k`, `t` and every pair of position sets\n`A, B \u2286 {0,\u2026,k\u22121}` with `|A| = |B|`, and every candidate set `S` that is a\nunion of residue classes mod `2^k`, the two bit-leak hints have identical class\nsize *multisets*, not merely identical sizes on the full cube.  Consequently a\nCoppersmith-style advantage of contiguous top-half leakage is invisible to any\ncounting argument and must be charged entirely to lattice reduction.\n\n*The key insight is* that \"position\" is an algorithmic resource, not an\ninformational one; the Coppersmith condition `t \u2265 k/2` cannot be recovered from\nany cardinality bound, which is why every attempt to beat it by re-arranging\nthe leaked bits has failed.\n\n*Why now?*  `card_fiber_coordRestrict_congr` proves the full-cube case in three\nlines; the general case is the statement that the two coordinate subgroups are\nconjugate under a permutation of the cube, which is within reach of Mathlib's\n`Equiv.Perm` API.",
