    "description": "`ImmortalityStructure.refinementStable_opow_iff` settles stability inside the scale `\u03c9 ^ a`.\nThe general statement should be:\n\n```lean\ntheorem refinementStable_iff_cnf (o : Ordinal) :\n    RefinementStable o \u2194 o = 0 \u2228 \u2200 e \u2208 (CNF \u03c9 o).map Prod.fst, \u03c9 \u2264 e\n```\n\ni.e. `\u03c9 \u00b7 o = o` exactly when every Cantor exponent of `o` is infinite.\n\n**The key insight is** that `\u03c9 \u00b7 o = o` is a *purely local* condition on the leading behaviour of\n`o`: multiplication by `\u03c9` shifts each Cantor exponent `e` to `1 + e`, and `1 + e = e` is\nequivalent to `\u03c9 \u2264 e`, so stability is a tail condition, not a size condition.\n\n**Why now?** Mathlib carries `Ordinal.CNF` with its induction principles, and the `\u03c9 ^ a` case is\nalready proved here, which fixes the exact form of the general criterion and its proof skeleton.\n\n---",
